\label{assump:aperiodic-unichain}
    The transition probability matrix $P_{{\sysbar{\pi}}^*}$ has a simple eigenvalue $1$; the other eigenvalues all have a modulus strictly smaller than $1$. In other words, $P_{{\sysbar{\pi}}^*}$ defines an aperiodic unichain on $\mathbb{S}$. 
    \footnote{A finite-state Markov chain is a unichain if it has a single-recurrent class, with possibly some transient states.}

\label{assump:non-degeneracy}
    For the fixed optimal solution to \eqref{eq:lp-single}, $y^*$, 
    there exists a unique \emph{neutral state}, i.e., a state $\tilde{s}\in\mathbb{S}$ s.t. $y^*(\tilde{s}, 1) > 0$ and $y^*(\tilde{s}, 0) > 0$.

\label{assump:local-stability}
