\end{align*}
Therefore, $h_{+}(X_t, [N]) > K_1 / \sqrt{N} + 2\lambda_{+}^{1/2} d_{\textup{IC}}(Y_t) / \beta + \lambda_{+}^{1/2}/(\beta N)$ implies $h_{+}(X_t, D_t) > K_1 / \sqrt{N}$; $\norm{X_t([N]) - \mu^*}_1 \leq \eta' -  6d_{\textup{IC}}(Y_t)/\beta - 3/(\beta N)$ implies that 
